{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal","id":323073,"title":"Please advise me on building a [2.5e] Sidereal.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-26T12:32:35-08:00","id":323073,"title":"Please advise me on building a [2.5e] Sidereal.","content":"Hey, Forum-goers. I've been out of Exalted for about a year now, trying to cool off and regroup after a multi-year campaign (my very first gig as ST, no less!). Now, as 3e creeps nearer, I think I'm ready to start getting back into Exalted, starting with a Heaven's Reach game I was invited to join.<br /> <br /> And since I love challenges, I'm looking to play a Sidereal for the first time ever. The only problem is that, even after reading MoEP: Sidereals, the Errata, Glories, and Shards, I still don't really know how effective their abilities are in an actual-play scenario, or how they will compare to my Solar and Lunar (T.A.W., to be precise) companions.<br /> <br /> I was hoping you fine folks might be able to offer up suggestions, anecdotes, and criticisms for a new Sidereal player, particularly regarding mechanical traps I might fall into, ways to get around some of the pitfalls that exist in Sidereal mechanics, and good synergies and strategies to take advantage of.<br /> <br /> Now, on to the specifics of my situation:<br /> <br /> My companions are a Solar hacker and gunslinger, the pilot of our little void-skipper and a god-empress-in-training. Her very alien Lunar &quot;son,&quot; who is an aspiring politico out to change the galactic status quo in a peaceful but definite manner. And my world-wise, easy-going Sidereal, posing as their mechanic/fixer/other allies as needed, keeping tabs on them and ensuring they don't blow up anything important. We have found a lost vault on a recently rediscovered planet, and are going to retrieve its contents. And that is all the players (myself included) know about the campaign.<br /> <br /> I've got basic 2.5e Character Creation to play with, and my choice of either regular Astrology or the Simple Astrology rules hack from Shards. I'd like to be something of a generalist, with a focus in Crafts (I'm the closest thing we have to a ship's mechanic), Performance (for Astrology and for tale-telling on long voyages), and maybe some investigative tricks. And perhaps most troubling, from what I've read, I'd actually like to try making heavy use of Astrology. I've even got a trick that my ST seems okay with, where I claim certain RD switches are a specialized form of summoning where the Sidereal &quot;fuses&quot; with a program-spirit from the Grand Celestial Mountain.<br /> <br /> So, how do I not die in combat? How do I avoid Paradox like the plague it is? What tricks would help me make and keep Destinies? Any good Artifacts or other Backgrounds that could help me keep up and be useful to my Circle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T13:57:30-08:00","id":323151,"title":"","content":"For defenses, it's hard to beat Sidereal Dodge. Duck Fate is one of the most comprehensive perfects in the game, and Absence can really get you out of a tight spot. If you'r elooking for offense in combat, then Melee, Archery, and Firearms are all decent, besides Martial Arts. I might also recommend you get into Sorcery, if neither of the others are.<br /> <br /> I'm afraid I can't help you with Astrology or Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T16:25:35-08:00","id":323228,"title":"","content":"Pardox is pretty easy to avoid astology is both really good and bad. If i remembered more about the system I'd go in more detail but im general don't both with giving opponents bad destinies just give yourself the really powerful dice modifier destinies as well as resplendencies like celestial bliss trick and everywhere and nowhere technique. Astrology can be stupid in the right combination but its also pretry boring. <br /> <br /> Sidereals have really good social manipulation charms. Poor but necessary defenses. Most of their non-MA just falls off at essence 4 to 5ish. Craft currently sucks extreme balls for them. They are almost as good a solars though. 2.5 fixed things but not everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T16:40:08-08:00","id":323232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal#post323073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how do I not die in combat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Grab some Resistance. You want Shield of Destiny and Optimistic Security Practice: it will give you soak, drain WP or Intimacies from your enemies, and cancel damage/return their attacks to them. Combined they won't make you win, but they'll make you too incredibly annoying to attack and incite opponents to focus on someone else. Then Duck Fate for a PD, because it's kind of amazing. Since you want to invest in Performance, I'd aim for Defense of Shining Joy as soon as you can. I would suggest investing in Medicine; it goes well with Mending Warped Design. If you ever get to that level, the capstone is one of the best around.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do I avoid Paradox like the plague it is? </div> </div> </div>There's little option for that beyond &quot;make sure to take a few months off here and there.&quot; Paradox drains off on its own, but slowly. You probably want to use Simple Astrology to minimize Paradox.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What tricks would help me make and keep Destinies? </div> </div> </div>First and Fateful Performance Excellency combined allow you to turn your entire Cha+Performance pool into successes, which should allow you to trivially succeed on astrology rolls using Simple Astrology. Canon Astrology is way moe complex, though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any good Artifacts or other Backgrounds that could help me keep up and be useful to my Circle? </div> </div> </div>There's a Hearthstone that boosts Performance rolls, magitech crafting implants, and various magical music instruments scattered across various books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T20:27:06-08:00","id":323365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You probably want to use Simple Astrology to minimize Paradox. </div> </div> </div>Wait, how is that possible ? You get 2 Paradox points for a failed roll, 5 for a botched, not everyone gonna have decent Cha/Per, except you also eat one point of Paradox for attaching a destiny to any Essence-user (INCLUDING yourself &gt;_&lt; ), not to mention Simple Astrology still keep the whole resplendent destiny's paradox. On one hand, this prevent abuses since nobody want to get hit Pattern Bite, on the other hand, it's feel kinda annoying that you can only use your splat special power once in a blue moon or your wife and your children gets hit by ice-cream bus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T20:35:55-08:00","id":323368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323365#post323365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, how is that possible ? You get 2 Paradox points for a failed roll, 5 for a botched, not everyone gonna have decent Cha/Per, except you also eat one point of Paradox for attaching a destiny to any Essence-user (INCLUDING yourself &gt;_&lt; ), not to mention Simple Astrology still keep the whole resplendent destiny's paradox. On one hand, this prevent abuses since nobody want to get hit Pattern Bite, on the other hand, it's feel kinda annoying that you can only use your splat special power once in a blue moon or your wife and your children gets hit by ice-cream bus.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're never going to fail an Astrology roll, because you'll be using the Fateful Performance Excellency!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T20:40:50-08:00","id":323371,"title":"","content":"Astrology is still pretty pointless/minor/XP sink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T21:01:03-08:00","id":323395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323371#post323371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astrology is still pretty pointless/minor/XP sink.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really want to have at least the ability to tag yourself (and ideally your allies) with an ascending Destiny, even more ideally under Simple Astrology. You just don't pass up a passive, costless -1 TN to a given set of actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-26T22:04:48-08:00","id":323420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323395#post323395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really want to have at least the ability to tag yourself (and ideally your allies) with an ascending Destiny, even more ideally under Simple Astrology. You just don't pass up a passive, costless -1 TN to a given set of actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, you're forgetting that tagging an Essence user under simple Astrology is an automatic point of Paradox, no roll, no save, do not pass Go. So your &quot;costless&quot; -1 TN is really costing you 5 Paradox, which need I remind you that Simple Astrology did nothing to modify or change, which was the REAL thing wrong with astrology. And the uselessness, but mostly the Paradox.<br /> <br /> Simple Astrology is, to be frank, shit, and no one should use it. If you really want to make Astrology &quot;simple,&quot; eliminate the prayer roll and just assume 1 -3 extra dice on the effect roll, depending on how big of a Cha + Per monkey you are.<br /> <br /> Redford, here are some of my suggestions. Note that several will probably require bribing your GM with food.<br /> <br /> -Roll Auspicious Prospects into one Charm, and make getting the caste aspects 1 XP repurchases. So you buy, say, Auspicious Prospects for Secrets, it's a normal Charm purchase. If you also want to pick up Auspicious Prospects for Endings, it only costs 1 XP. This fixes the problem of Auspicious Prospects being disgustingly over priced.<br /> <br /> Second, change Auspicious Prospects so that a Maiden may activate it remotely to give a Sidereal a &quot;bonus goal&quot; for the scene, according to their whims and grand designs for Fate (ie things the GM would like to see happen). The Sidereal is under no compulsion to achieve these goals, but if they do, they dissipate a point of Paradox at the end of the scene. This gives another avenue to dissipate Paradox (and you need as many of those as you can get) and fixes the problem of Auspicious Problems not actually fucking doing anything.<br /> <br /> -Efficient Secretary Technique (Also known as the Google Spider) is one of the best Charms in the game. Even nerfed in the errata, it's still incredibly powerful and lets you know all kinds of things you have no business knowing.<br /> <br /> -Methodology of Secrets is one of my personal favorites and, I think, fairly underrated. You can be an expert in damn near anything with a power nap.<br /> <br /> -Beg, borrow, plead, kidnap your GM's dog, whatever it takes, but get your GM to put something, <i>anything</i> in place of the current Paradox system. The current Paradox system is desgined to fuck you, the player, over, not create interesting stories. If your GM doesn't believe that, ask them how useful it would be to their game if your character was completely unable to get Essence back for 9 days. That's one of the tamer effects.<br /> <br /> -Since you mentioned Craft, the one Charm that lets you move things (and whose name I can't recall at the moment) is shit. While you're bribing your GM, see if they'll replace it with Celestial Drifter's Panoply from <i>Shards</i>, which is much, much better. Or, if you're already using that tree since it's a Heaven's Reach game, see if they'll replace it with another Charm, or just a picture of a plastic green dinosaur. It'd be better.<br /> <br /> -If you're looking for the most mechanical benefit, than Secrets, Endings and Serenity are the only castes you should consider. Secrets and Endings each give you one of your One True Skills (Occult and Martial Arts, respectively) as caste for free; assuming Heaven's Reach is like the default setting, Sorcery and Martial Arts are the only skills you can freely develop new Charms for. Serenity's anima power means you don't have to spend a Charm purchase on a Performance excellency for astrology.<br /> <br /> Might be more...I really need to get my big list o' Sidereal advice written down in one place somewhere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T08:26:26-08:00","id":323640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323420#post323420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, you're forgetting that tagging an Essence user under simple Astrology is an automatic point of Paradox, no roll, no save, do not pass Go. So your &quot;costless&quot; -1 TN is really costing you 5 Paradox, which need I remind you that Simple Astrology did nothing to modify or change, which was the REAL thing wrong with astrology. And the uselessness, but mostly the Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>...so what? 5 Paradox to give five people a passive -1 TN is pretty good, given that, again, you can get rid of Paradox. The only point that matters is the last, and before that dread, character-destroying point, you can just... stop using Resplendencies and making ascending destinies while you get rid of it. <br /> <br /> I've never had a single Paradox event in a year and change of playing a Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:00:48-08:00","id":323657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323640#post323640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...so what? 5 Paradox to give five people a passive -1 TN is pretty good, given that, again, you can get rid of Paradox. The only point that matters is the last, and before that dread, character-destroying point, you can just... stop using Resplendencies and making ascending destinies while you get rid of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the <i>automatic</i> Paradox you get. You're still looking at rolling probably at least three dice or so for each roll. Remember that 10s count as two!<br /> <br /> You must just play a much more sedate game than I do if you can really just lay some ascending destinties and then just not use astrology at all for months on end. I imagine you must never use resplendency powers as well, since most of them churn up the Paradox. What can I say? I find having an active Key resplendency so I have an emergency Yu-Shan bolt hole available if I need it is super useful. And sometimes you just need to lay an emergency destiny on the Lap <i>right fucking now.</i><br /> <br /> I don't think &quot;Sidereals just sit around and smoke weed for six months every time they use astrology&quot; is a good assumption to be designing the system around.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:13:22-08:00","id":323662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323657#post323657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the <i>automatic</i> Paradox you get. You're still looking at rolling probably at least three dice or so for each roll. Remember that 10s count as two!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">In addition to the usual methods for gaining Paradox<br /> from <u><b>resplendent</b></u> destinies, Sidereals suffer two points<br /> of Paradox for a failed astrology roll of either variety,<br /> and five Paradox for a botched astrology roll. Sidereals<br /> also suffer a <u><b>single</b></u> point of paradox for attaching an<br /> ascending or descending destiny to an Essence-user<br /> (including themselves).</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>The first clause adds to resplendent Paradox; the second clause <i>supercedes</i> ascending/descending Paradox. You only get one Paradox for making ascending destinies, ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You must just play a much more sedate game than I do if you can really just lay some ascending destinties and then just not use astrology at all for months on end. I imagine you must never use resplendency powers as well, since most of them churn up the Paradox. What can I say? I find having an active Key resplendency so I have an emergency Yu-Shan bolt hole available if I need it is super useful. And sometimes you just need to lay an emergency destiny on the Lap <i>right fucking now.</i> </div> </div> </div>It's Modern, so the emergency bolt is useless (Yu-Shan is, uh, basically Mogadicci). I use mostly the Shield bonus for soak, the surprise-negator in the Sword, the astrology-boosting one in Sorcerer, and Privacy-Enhancing Gesture. None of these cost Paradox. It's not even for that reason that I use them, they just tend to be the most conveient for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T09:54:49-08:00","id":323698,"title":"","content":"I find the regular astrology rules working not so bad, except for the fact that they can take quite a long time of plannning (both in game and IRL).<br /> <br /> And unless you really have horrible cha+perf, I don't think you really NEED an excellency in perf. Using WP for one success, equipement bonus (+1 dice), extended prayer (+3 dice), stunt dice (not hard to get +2), speciality with methodology of secrets (+3 dice), petition (variable bonuses), priest hood bonus (already accounted for when they say diff 6 i guess) etc... I find is enough<br /> <br /> But the one charm I would totally recommend (using normal astrology rules) is methodology of secrets. If allows you to boost your rolls for every &quot;secondary&quot; element as long as you delay each aspect (anyway astrology is never en emergency element so it doesn't hurt really). Want to make a petition? get a speciality of caligraphy in linguistics and get a free +3 on your roll. Want to compute astrology and design fate plans to help your effect roll? get a speciality in occult/craft to help. It even boosts the effect roll for a college if you put a fitting speciality in the ability associated with it.<br /> <br /> The only thing I negociate with my GM is that the &quot;ritual behavior&quot; bonus (p.208 MoEP : sid) can be accomplished without having to don a resplendent destily of the college, because that puts a heavy logistic to unlock it (especially if you want to create a resplendent destiny, in which case you create first a &quot;disposable&quot; one just to get the ritual behavior bonus and you discard it right before creating the &quot;real&quot; resplendent destiny as you can only have one in each college)<br /> <br /> Also, my last advice XP-wise, don't bother geting above 1-2 dots in colleges. Having 1 dot in each college with interesting resplendencies is important. The 2nd dot is quite cheap, especially for the in-house ones. Above, it really makes little difference given the XP invested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T11:34:21-08:00","id":323782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323662#post323662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first clause adds to resplendent Paradox; the second clause <i>supercedes</i> ascending/descending Paradox. You only get one Paradox for making ascending destinies, ever. </div> </div> </div>That is false. The clause you quoted is for attaching a destiny, which is the second part of putting an additional charge of one Paradox on. <i>Making</i> the destiny is the roll, which is what triggers the Paradox roll and which Simple Astrology does not modify. It goes thusly:<br /> <br /> 1. Make roll to craft the destiny<br /> 2. Make Paradox roll for crafting destiny<br /> 3. Attach destiny to target (which Simple Astrology adds an additional cost of 1 Paradox to)<br /> <br /> If your table has houseruled that the point of Paradox given for attaching a destiny supersedes the Paradox roll, that's fine, but that's not in the system as written and that's not (as far as we know) the option Redford is being given. Simple Astrology as written is by far objectively worse for the player than regular Astrology because it gives out far more Paradox for doing far less with the system. Thus it cannot be recommended for anyone. I joke about Sidereals being for masochistic players, but I don't actually want it to be <i>true</i>.<br /> <br /> Edit: And that's not even getting into the other problems of Simple Astrology, like how you never actually get any better at it at least as far as putting destinities on Exalts (since it's based on Essence and, as a Sidereal, your Excellency is also based on Essence), and the hideously long time it takes to do <i>anything</i> with it (12 hour base interval plus an <i>entire day</i> per <i>one</i> extra die?). Regular astrology could take a lot of in-game time as well, but that was <i>optional</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","user":"Coik","date":". 11-27-2014, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T12:34:10-08:00","id":323819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323782#post323782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your table has houseruled that the point of Paradox given for attaching a destiny supersedes the Paradox roll, that's fine, but that's not in the system as written and that's not (as far as we know) the option Redford is being given. Simple Astrology as written is by far objectively worse for the player than regular Astrology because it gives out far more Paradox for doing far less with the system. Thus it cannot be recommended for anyone. I joke about Sidereals being for masochistic players, but I don't actually want it to be <i>true</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how incredibly annoying and irritating it is when you're engaged in a discussion over differing interpretations of a text, and then someone pulls the &quot;it's fine if you're houseruling it, but I'm talking about the<i> real rules</i>&quot; card? It's so annoying and condescending, instead of further engaging this argument I will just sit there and laugh at you for actively misinterpreting the rules in a way that actually makes them worse for you, just so you can justify your continued hate-on ^_^ You're like a reverse munchkin!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-27T16:57:24-08:00","id":323957,"title":"","content":"I'd ask if your rating in a given Ability also counts as the rating of the College that the Ability is tied to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T02:14:47-08:00","id":324320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323819#post323819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how incredibly annoying and irritating it is when you're engaged in a discussion over differing interpretations of a text, and then someone pulls the &quot;it's fine if you're houseruling it, but I'm talking about the<i> real rules</i>&quot; card? It's so annoying and condescending, instead of further engaging this argument I will just sit there and laugh at you for actively misinterpreting the rules in a way that actually makes them worse for you, just so you can justify your continued hate-on ^_^ You're like a reverse munchkin!</div> </div> </div> </div>haha, your message reminds me of a small exalted comic in the BD book I guess. It was like 2 immaculate monks face to face basically saying :<br /> - I saw you kill [that other guy] just because he had a diffrent interpretation of the immaculate texts<br /> - you're wrong!<br /> - What? I saw you kill him with your own hands<br /> - No, you're wrong because there is no such thing as the interpretation of the texts<br /> <br /> Also, my 2 cents on this subject :<br /> The prayer and effect roll for a destiny create it but it stays dormant until you touch the person it's intended to. And the paradox is the reflection, not so of the little effort that it takes to create the identity/blessing/curse but how to maintain it in function in the long run (especially in the case of the identity, when you act in contradiction with it).<br /> <br /> Now in the original rules, as paradox was rolled, they probably figured since you already roll for prayer and effect points, why not roll directly the paradox in the process and be done with it (so you're sure you didn't forget it). In the simple astrology, since it's not rolled I think they just moved the paradox aquisition to the moment it entered in effect which is more accurate I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T02:34:53-08:00","id":324332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=323957#post323957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd ask if your rating in a given Ability also counts as the rating of the College that the Ability is tied to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally since 2.5 the only thing I'd change about the costs of College ratings is to lower the Out-of-House costs to be less punitive if you want access to an effect from a caste that nobody is playing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T03:44:12-08:00","id":324374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324332#post324332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally since 2.5 the only thing I'd change about the costs of College ratings is to lower the Out-of-House costs to be less punitive if you want access to an effect from a caste that nobody is playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I find the best solution would be to group all colleges in the same house so you have a totalof 5 ratings instead of having a full page of 25 diferent ratings to keep track of and 80% of them are at 0 (for most non-specialised chars).<br /> <br /> Then you have to rebalance the XP cost (maybe to the original 2ed cost), and change how many starting dots you have.<br /> <br /> Finally since you would get a system that isn't an XP sink, doesn't have a ton of diferent ratings... the only &quot;problem&quot; left to solve is how the 1st dot is important and the others are almost irrelevant. I would say unlock the respendecies, and higher frequencies/durations for destines at higher ratings, and maybe allow for using excellencies to boost effect rolls in the associated college but with a dicecap of [college rating].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":2172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","user":"Jack In The Box","date":". 11-28-2014, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T07:32:25-08:00","id":324482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324374#post324374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally since you would get a system that isn't an XP sink, doesn't have a ton of diferent ratings... the only &quot;problem&quot; left to solve is how the 1st dot is important and the others are almost irrelevant. I would say unlock the respendecies, and higher frequencies/durations for destines at higher ratings, and maybe allow for using excellencies to boost effect rolls in the associated college but with a dicecap of [college rating].</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I see with that is Sidereals are already severely handicapped in their Exellencies, since they're tied to Essence. Saying that you need to raise Essence <i>and</i> Colleges to improve your Excellencies is needlessly restrictive and doesn't really do anything to take away the feeling that Colleges are an XP tax. The entire problem with Astrology, generally speaking, is that it's about 50:1 stick/carrot as it is, I don't really see wrapping up a meaningful sense of progression in it as changing that.<br /> <br /> The thing is, this wouldn't be perceived as &quot;I raise my Colleges and I get to use my Excellencies better,&quot; it will be seen as &quot;I have to raise my Colleges to use my Excellencies better.&quot; Particularly since no other Exalt has to jump through that kind of hoop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then you have to rebalance the XP cost (maybe to the original 2ed cost), and change how many starting dots you have. </div> </div> </div>I don't know how serious I want to be about arguing that Colleges are actually a character flaw and, as such, you shouldn't be <i>paying</i> anything for them. Rather, the system should be giving you build points and/or XP for taking them, since they obviously significantly disadvantage you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T10:10:04-08:00","id":324621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324482#post324482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem I see with that is Sidereals are already severely handicapped in their Exellencies, since they're tied to Essence. Saying that you need to raise Essence <i>and</i> Colleges to improve your Excellencies is needlessly restrictive and doesn't really do anything to take away the feeling that Colleges are an XP tax. The entire problem with Astrology, generally speaking, is that it's about 50:1 stick/carrot as it is, I don't really see wrapping up a meaningful sense of progression in it as changing that.<br /> <br /> The thing is, this wouldn't be perceived as &quot;I raise my Colleges and I get to use my Excellencies better,&quot; it will be seen as &quot;I have to raise my Colleges to use my Excellencies better.&quot; Particularly since no other Exalt has to jump through that kind of hoop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since its an addition to the base functionality of excellencies, you can admit it can only be an improvement. Now it doesn't mean that it fits your character's concept.<br /> <br /> For someone that wants to play the &quot;astrology specialist&quot; sid, It can be apealing to get a high rating in a few important colleges and being able to get [college] aditional automatic successes on his effect roll with an excellecy.<br /> <br /> Also if you switch from a system with independent ratings for each college to a system where all 5 colleges on a house have the same, you're literally dividing by 5 the PX sink/tax, which (more or less) should be at least a huge step in the right direction.<br /> <br /> If you really don't like it well, maybe having your college rating reduce the number of paradox dice you roll when creating a destiny? Kills 2 birds with one stone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324482#post324482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know how serious I want to be about arguing that Colleges are actually a character flaw and, as such, you shouldn't be <i>paying</i> anything for them. Rather, the system should be giving you build points and/or XP for taking them, since they obviously significantly disadvantage you.</div> </div> </div> </div>you're paying for virtues, and they still impact your character flow...<br /> <br /> Also,colleges by themstlves are not a flaw. Colleges allow you tu use an aspect of the sid's exclusive powers that, in turn, under some conditions, can backfire horribly.<br /> <br /> One thing I find stupid is that one of the aspect of paradox is being a &quot;speed limit&quot; to prevent too frequent missuse of astrology, but the way it was designed is bad at the job :<br /> - it's basically scews you so much whenever you're doing anything important that you will be extremely careful, so you never get bitten in such conditions<br /> - also it's such a huge threat and it decays so slowly (even if you accelerate it with warped fly ritual), that whenever you have a &quot;downtime&quot; and you're high on paradox you'ld consider intentionally hitting 10 and getting rid of it<br /> <br /> If I could give advice to devs, it would be something along these lines:<br /> - when you hit 10 paradox, it doesn't reset to 0 and you don't get a instantaneous (+short term) handicap<br /> - instead you have to make it drop down to 0 yourself (and then possibly an additional fixed duration afterwards so that the spiders' wrath calms) and during that time you get a (kinda) minor handicap (nowhere near the pattern spider venom effects), possibly just &quot;the pattern spiders ignore all your new requests, your boons and curses stop taking effect, you can use existing resplendent destinies but not the associated respendencies&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T12:04:54-08:00","id":324713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324621#post324621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you're paying for virtues, and they still impact your character flow...</div> </div> </div> </div>(1) Not really as much of a flaw since they're not going to affect your personality if you don't want them to and still have choice as to their expression;<br /> (2) Higher Virtues can be a significantly useful resource.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T13:56:21-08:00","id":324779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324713#post324713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(1) Not really as much of a flaw since they're not going to affect your personality if you don't want them to and still have choice as to their expression;<br /> (2) Higher Virtues can be a significantly useful resource.</div> </div> </div> </div>(1) I don't agree :<br /> - even if you CAN act against your high virtues, you pay WP and accrue limit...<br /> - and given that you can't reliably reduce your limit,you end up in limit break<br /> - even ignoring these mechanisms, 3+ virtues can be abused in social combat to reduce your MDVs by 2<br /> <br /> (2) astrology is also a useful ressource if you prepareit in advance and adapt to your mission. Even if you put aside dice-roll altering curses and boons you still have :<br /> - bonus WP regeneration, very useful for sids (&amp; allies)<br /> - conditional virtue altering (possibly reducing your compassion in situations you don't want to be the nice guy etc... possibilities are almost endless)<br /> - alternate identities with free +3 bonus dice to convince people or explain incoherent element, and they get -3internal penality<br /> - &quot;free&quot; dice bonus (not counting for charm dice caps I guess?) and 3rd excellencies in most social situations and for stealth. Doesn't count as charm usage (huge bonus pre 2.5) and probably won't show up for anyone with magic/essence detection<br /> - &quot;free&quot; perfect social soak, doesn't count as charm usage (same advantages as above)<br /> - &quot;I point at you and your temporary WP is reduced to your [conviction] rating if it was higher&quot;. Fucks up people in a lot of situations, particularily in social combat.Don't forget you can curse enemies to reduce their conviction under specific circumstances like &quot;in my presence&quot;. Only 1 paradox dice<br /> - &quot;i instantly turn into a bird&quot; AKA we stole one of the most useful power of lunars, and we even get to frame them for it while we look innocent &quot;hey it can't be me who did it. I can't shapeshift, I dunno that spell and even if I could I would turn into a flock of them, not just ONE bird&quot;<br /> - Reflexive perfect protection against memory altering effects<br /> - secure and instantaneous mail delivery between sidereals<br /> - scenelong +9L/+9B natural soak, doesn't count as charm usage<br /> - instantaneous scenelong scry and teleportation-proof zone<br /> <br /> And there are a few other ones","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The fool can only learn from a sage, but only the sage can learn from a fool.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2172-jack-in-the-box","name":"Jack In The Box","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T19:43:46-08:00","id":324981,"title":"","content":"<b>War Dragon</b>, <b>Epimetheus</b>, <b>Zelbinnean</b>, <b>Lioness</b>, thank you for popping in here to share your thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>Jen</b>, thank you for the artwork in your Sidereal threads. It really helped me to imagine how Sidereal players feel. Especially that picture with Asna Firstborn getting jumped by angry Sids...<br /> <br /> <b>Coik</b>, <b>Omicron</b>, <b>Jack in the Box</b>, you folks are awesome, and I'm loving the different perspectives you are sharing. Thank you so much. I've got some questions and ideas that follow from stuff you've said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324320#post324320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">haha, your message reminds me of a small exalted comic in the BD book I guess. It was like 2 immaculate monks face to face basically saying :<br /> - I saw you kill [that other guy] just because he had a diffrent interpretation of the immaculate texts<br /> - you're wrong!<br /> - What? I saw you kill him with your own hands<br /> - No, you're wrong because there is no such thing as the interpretation of the texts</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, yes, a classic example of Peleps Deled! Some of the old chapter comics were really good.<br /> <br /> My understanding of Paradox gain from Simple Astrology is that it produces less than equivalent Classic Astrology. I did some theorizing, and spoilered it right below. My conclusion (and please tell me if you disagree) is this: Classic Astrology requires more explicit preparation, and can give more Paradox, but has a more varied range of powerful effects (rapid Willpower gain/loss, OMG!). Simple Astrology loses versatility and power, but is a little faster and produces less Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> My best reading of Simple Astrology is that Ascending/Descending Destinies only give 1 point of Paradox when applied to an Essence-user (so, 3 points to buff my current 3-person Circle), and nothing more (unless you fail or botch the roll). Meanwhile, the only Paradox gained from Resplendent Destinies seems to come from straining the identity with Resplendency Powers or breaking character.<br /> <br /> I did a quick comparison with normal Astrology, and came up with something like 4 Paradox <i>dice</i> per Ascending/Descending Destiny, assuming it covered the same Trigger/Scope/Duration/Frequency. If you increased the Scope to hit the whole Circle at once, you don't gain any extra Paradox, but the Effect Points needed jump from 8 (4 Frequency, 3 Essence Burden, 1 Duration) to 14 (+6 Essence Burden). Considering the best (min-maxed) pool I can currently build for the Effect Roll would be 16 dice... my chances of success are pretty slim.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, my min-maxed dice pool for Simple Astrology would be something like 19 dice (which Simple Astrology does not explicitly prevent from being converted to Auspicious Successes), against a Difficulty of 7 (self or Circle-mate). I could well get 12 effect points there.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> While I hate to lose some of the power that comes with Classic Astrology, I think Simple Astrology gives me a better chance for high rates of success, particularly when it comes to Resplendent Destinies, which I think are the more interesting parts of Astrology as it currently exists.<br /> <br /> So, my next questions revolve around synergies and workarounds. For example, could I use Embracing Life Method in my personal library in Yu-Shan, then reasonably make use of my Google-Spider or Research Assistant Invocation to harvest the clues remotely, rather than have to go all the way back to Yu-Shan? What do you think about my idea of disguising Resplendent Destinies as &quot;summoning/fusing&quot; with spirits, to help explain away the sudden disappearance of the engineer, and the equally sudden appearance of someone completely different?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-28T21:52:33-08:00","id":325063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redford_Blade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324981#post324981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my next questions revolve around synergies and workarounds. For example, could I use Embracing Life Method in my personal library in Yu-Shan, then reasonably make use of my Google-Spider or Research Assistant Invocation to harvest the clues remotely, rather than have to go all the way back to Yu-Shan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Google Spider I would say no, since it's more of an Essence construct than a truly sentient being. Fern-friend Research Assistants I would say would be able to harvest ELM answers and place them in your personal library, which you could then retrieve with Google Spider.<br /> <br /> This is also a good opportunity to mention two house rules we used in my last game: first, Research Assistants didn't have a duration, existing until dismissed, killed, or what have you. While my character was the type who would return to Yu-Shan several times a week anyway to take care of her In box, that way I could start long research projects without being <i>obligated</i> to head back to Yu-Shan every five days to renew the Charm.<br /> <br /> We also ruled that any Sidereal in good standing with Heaven could count the Forbidding Manse of Ivy's collection of materials as part of &quot;their&quot; personal library, and thus asscessible through Google Spider. Secrets caste had further access to some lightly restricted materials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do you think about my idea of disguising Resplendent Destinies as &quot;summoning/fusing&quot; with spirits, to help explain away the sudden disappearance of the engineer, and the equally sudden appearance of someone completely different? </div> </div> </div>I'm fairly ambivilant to it, at least partially due to unfamiliarity with Heaven's Reach. I actually haven't read any of the Shards, so I'm not familiar with the specifics of the setting assumptions made. (I skimmed one...Modern, I think?...and it looked like the Infernal wanking off that was typical of late 2e, so I skipped all the rest) In the default setting I don't think it's be particularly necessary, as Arcane Fate would mean most people would forget that the resplendency identity existed in the first place before too long.<br /> <br /> Don't really know if Arcane Fate is a thing in Heaven's Reach, but if it isn't I feel like that would be a shame, since I think it's one of the most blatantly entertaining things about playing a Sidereal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T11:33:48-08:00","id":332357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=325063#post325063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly ambivilant to it, at least partially due to unfamiliarity with Heaven's Reach. I actually haven't read any of the Shards, so I'm not familiar with the specifics of the setting assumptions made. (I skimmed one...Modern, I think?...and it looked like the Infernal wanking off that was typical of late 2e, so I skipped all the rest) In the default setting I don't think it's be particularly necessary, as Arcane Fate would mean most people would forget that the resplendency identity existed in the first place before too long.<br /> <br /> Don't really know if Arcane Fate is a thing in Heaven's Reach, but if it isn't I feel like that would be a shame, since I think it's one of the most blatantly entertaining things about playing a Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to take so long to reply! Work has been so hectic this week that I might as well have activated Invisible At the Center!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: Sidereals, pg. 196</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She must be in a state of virtual slavery, sleeping at the job and living only to perform, and has only seven free hours per week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcane Fate is indeed still a thing in Heaven's Reach (which I recommend taking a second look at, as well as the rest of Shards; the Infernal &quot;taint&quot; in Modern is entirely necessary, to create an Exalted equivalent of the World of Darkness that your heroes can rebel against).<br /> <br /> But while Arcane Fate exists in Heaven's Reach, my understanding and experience has been that Exalts become largely resistant to it, and beings outside Fate are immune. And since the plot we are following will involve being the only crew on an isolated starship, surrounded by alien demons and space fae, I was worried that there was no way to use my Resplendent Destinies without my fellow Exalts asking unfortunate questions, like &quot;Where is my engineer?&quot; and &quot;Who the hell are you!?&quot;<br /> <br /> The understanding I have with the ST is that I will still have to deal with Arcane Fate, such as when I am not using a Destiny or a Destiny ends, but that I can more safely use my Resplendent Destinies in the presence of the other PCs without immediately risking Paradox, as their suspicions are allayed by claims of &quot;sorcery&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T03:24:01-08:00","id":334069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack In The Box</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/323073-please-advise-me-on-building-a-2-5e-sidereal?p=324374#post324374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I find the best solution would be to group all colleges in the same house so you have a totalof 5 ratings instead of having a full page of 25 diferent ratings to keep track of and 80% of them are at 0 (for most non-specialised chars).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just never found solutions for removing the colleges very satisfying.<br /> <br /> In the Sidereal game I'm currently in there's two PC Chosen of Journeys, mine favours the Gull while the other favours the Messenger these are rather telling about their personalities and preferences. Similarly the ability connection doesn't work for me because I like the Gull for it's whole freedom of the wanderer aspect which doesn't translate into Thrown (she's actually a Martial Arts kickgirl because her boots weren't just made for walking).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}